<title>POLAND: Poland to import 200,000 T of grain in Q1 1997.</title>
<headline>Poland to import 200,000 T of grain in Q1 1997.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland will import 200,000 tonnes of grain to increase its operational reserves in the first quarter of this year, the government's economic council said in a statement late on Monday.</p>
<p>It said the imports were already being realised but gave no figures. Poland imported some 1.9 million tonnes of grain in the fourth quarter of last year, most of which found its way to the market after a supply shortage caused by bad harvests.</p>
<p>The imports also boosted operational reserves by some 320,000 tonnes at the end of 1996, it said.</p>
<p>Poland's operational reserves are used to intervene on domestic grain markets when the supply of grain dwindles and prices rise quickly.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
